        {
          "id": "note",
          "kind": "note",
          "data": {
            "text": "## HF station\n\nTwo decoders on one radio. **FT8** and **WSPR** both run from the same Device, because one HF radio can carry several narrow decoders at once.\n\n**Propagation map** turns their decodes into where the signals came from, which is the point of listening to either. It needs **GPS position** to know where the other end of each path is.\n\n**Event filter** sits between the decoders and the log. Empty, it keeps everything. Add a callsign to `stations` and the log holds only that station.\n\n**Decoder log** keeps what got through the filter.\n\nTuned to 20m FT8 at 14.074 MHz. Move the Device for another band; both decoders follow."
          },
